You're thinking

00:04:21.273 --> 00:04:22.150
about it now.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.350
This is a better delivery.
No, just take a beat.

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:25.810
I got it.
And think about

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.003
how you wanna tell your story.
There was one thing that I

00:04:28.003 --> 00:04:28.980
needed to change.
I'm just gonna stare at ya.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.830
Well, I'm not figuring it
out, I'm just gonna continue

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:31.800
telling the story.
Okay.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.950
So you know how I'm

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:39.220
gonna make my pool slash
backyard area better than yours?

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.970
That's what I'm doing in 2020.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.300
Yeah 'cause it hasn't been for--

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.690
Right, yeah.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:44.690
A number of years.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.383
Yeah.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.200
I'm in the process of doing
that, before I make it better

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.610
than Link's, what I have
to do is I have to make it

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:56.152
worse than it is because I
have to demolish it, right?

00:04:56.152 --> 00:04:58.610
You have to make it
unenjoyable, totally unlivable.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:02.863
Currently, it is in a
completely deconstructed state.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.450
They just tore everything
down and basically piled it

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.350
in a corner, the guys have
gone into the pool and like,

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.550
jack hammered off the
surface so it just kinda

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.730
looks like a post apocalyptic scene.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:15.730
I bet you like that.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:18.113
In my yard area.

00:05:19.325 --> 00:05:23.580
And of course I'm still making
decisions about some of the

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:28.470
final design points and where
things are gonna go and so

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.320
I just went out there yesterday

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:37.460
and I'm just like, I mean, I
was probably just out there

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:40.769
just standing and kinda just
looking, standing in one place

00:05:40.769 --> 00:05:44.830
and looking at different
things and just thinking.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:47.580
Visualizing the future.
For five to seven minutes.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:49.543
All of a sudden,

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:51.513
I hear,

00:05:53.087 --> 00:05:54.917
"You got a mess down there."

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.823
And then I was like, God, is that you?

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.647
I was like, "You're right."

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.810
Was it that echo-y and boomy?

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.330
It came from on high.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:09.163
Okay.

00:06:09.163 --> 00:06:12.393
It came from above me
which freaked me out a lot.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:15.120
'Cause I've lived in
this house for four years

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.970
and this has never happened.
Yeah.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:19.450
So I look to the skies.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:20.283
You looked up.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:25.210
And I didn't see the clouds
part, what I saw is a man

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:29.040
standing, now this is what
I was about to say, but now

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:30.590
I was able to tell the
story in a funny way,

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:33.160
now I'm gonna tell you, I'm
gonna orient you in a way

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.550
that you'll understand where
this voice was coming from.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:39.203
So as is typical when
you kinda live on a hill,

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:45.140
sometimes, like so I live
at this spot on the hill

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:48.250
and then like, my backyard is
basically almost a vertical

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:51.950
wall of earth that goes up
and then other people's yards

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:56.730
start, their backyards are
all looking the same way and--

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:58.770
Terraced above you.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.390
Yeah and so there are
people who live up there and

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:04.280
I've like driven on the road
that runs parallel to my road

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.850
and I can like, I don't know these people,

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:08.570
we've never had any interactions.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:09.403
Yeah.

00:07:09.403 --> 00:07:11.127
Except for one older
couple on the other side,

00:07:11.127 --> 00:07:13.130
right when we moved in
they were up there kind of

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:15.670
looking off into the distance
and we talked to them

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:19.410
but this guy's like--
Did they think you were

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.530
Satan when you looked up at 'em and said,

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:25.010
got a mess up there, they
looked down thinking you were--

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.100
Nope, I just said--
Beelzebub?

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:29.680
I just said, "Oh hey."

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:34.360
'Cause basically at the
top of the wall of dirt or

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:38.261
plantage of sorts, there's
like people's fences, right?

00:07:38.261 --> 00:07:39.094
Yeah.

00:07:39.094 --> 00:07:41.610
And so right in the middle
of my lot, there is,

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.430
two people's houses, like,
there lot's gonna come together

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:47.290
so that their lots meet and
split kinda where my lot is

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:49.930
so I can see two people's yards up there.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:52.500
So one of the yards, this
guy's standing in the corner.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:53.630
You got two gods.

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:56.087
And he is like--

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:58.747
Got a mess down there.
I was like,

00:07:58.747 --> 00:08:01.937
"Oh hey," he was like, "I'm Ken."

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:05.707
I was like, "I'm Rhett."

00:08:07.251 --> 00:08:08.418
Okay.
And--

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:14.210
So he said, "Got a mess down
there," you said, "Oh okay."

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.072
I was like--
And then you said, "Oh Ken."

00:08:16.072 --> 00:08:19.450
No, I was like, "Yeah, got a
lot of work to do down here,

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:20.920
just gettin' started," or whatever,

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:23.530
you know, just typical BS.

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:25.460
I would've said, get
down here, get to work.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:28.220
And it was a little unsettling because,

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:29.500
let me tell you why this was unsettling.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:30.333
Okay.

00:08:30.333 --> 00:08:33.790
Because I know I just was
like, talking like this

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:37.580
but then we proceeded to have
a conversation at this volume.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.950
Talking this loud, I wasn't
yelling at him, I was on the

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:45.260
other side of my, like, across
the pool from him and he's

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.820
all the way up there and
we're just talking at this

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:52.390
volume right here, what did
that immediately make me think?

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:56.270
That, I have no clue, that like you have

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.690
super human hearing and he can't hear you?

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:00.370
And I don't know if
this, I don't if you've

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:02.160
thought this but it made me think that--

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:03.950
Oh, I know, that he's heard every

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:05.650
conversation you've had in your backyard.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:06.790
Yes.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:07.700
Yes.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.750
And I had this sense of absolute

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.384
privacy in my backyard because--

00:09:11.384 --> 00:09:13.810
Oh you've been saying
some private stuff, huh?

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:14.900
Well--
I've been back there

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:15.900
for some private stuff.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:16.960
Well I'm just sayin'.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.160
I mean conversations.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.315
It made me think that,

00:09:21.315 --> 00:09:24.560
some neighbors kind of off on one,

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.287
the way the houses come
together is very odd 'cause

00:09:26.287 --> 00:09:29.810
we're all on this hill and
so, you know, on one side

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.340
of my pool I've got like
that giant ivy wall.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.200
That's actually what I was
looking at, there's this giant,

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:37.140
there's a fence and then like
an ivy wall but we've taken

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:41.150
down the awning, the roof
part and now I can kinda like

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:43.710
see through parts of the ivy
and I can see, oh there's a

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:46.640
house right there and their
backyard comes up to right here

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:49.450
and like, they have a little
area that they can sit and

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.810
they were sitting right there
while I was in my hot tub

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.993
like having a conversation
with my friends about whatever.

00:09:58.683 --> 00:10:00.035
They could just sit
out there and listen to

00:10:00.035 --> 00:10:00.868
the whole thing.
They could just listen.

00:10:00.868 --> 00:10:02.150
Effortlessly.

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:04.830
Them even more so but then Ken,

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:05.980
he could just come to the corner,

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:07.650
I would never see Ken in the corner.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:12.030
Or Ken could put out
like a recording device

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:13.270
and he'd just have it all.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.030
What if he has a Whisper 2000?

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:16.440
Sounds like he doesn't need one.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:18.910
But if he did, he could
point it right at me.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:21.323
Yeah, Whisper 2000.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:25.270
Hey Ken, you got a Whisper 2000 up there?

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.980
Do they still have Whisper 2000?

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.007
I barely know what that is.
Jenna could you

00:10:28.007 --> 00:10:29.100
look that up?
That's like a megaphone

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.383
you aim at stuff so you
can hear the conversations.

00:10:31.383 --> 00:10:32.600
I always wanted one.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:33.800
It's like a spy device.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.990
My family and I used to
joke about the Whisper 2000.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.440
So often, it's the kind of thing that

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.010
my dad would really latch onto.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:41.020
Yeah, he was really into that.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:43.213
Making jokes about the Whisper 2000

00:10:43.213 --> 00:10:45.644
because it had a name, Whisper 2000.

00:10:45.644 --> 00:10:46.644
Is it still a thing?

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:49.193
It looks like--

00:10:49.193 --> 00:10:50.676
She's not finding that it's still a thing.

00:10:50.676 --> 00:10:53.050
Well, let me see--
Whisper 2000's not a thing?

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.290
Anyway.
So what,

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:55.870
you're talking to Ken,
you're thinking this

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:58.080
at the time or you reflected upon this?

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.270
No, I was thinking at
the time, I was like--

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:02.190
I'm not having to raise my voice at all.

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:04.670
Not only that but like, you know,

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:07.120
anything that I've said, even the

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.290
things I've said in my house,

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:11.860
like with the windows
open, you know, sometimes

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.140
the windows are open which at that point

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:15.830
I'm basically even with
him in the second story and

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.260
you know, the times that
we've gotten in fights,

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.780
