00:39:21.610 --> 00:39:24.500
to get and what we have found,
it's a general principle,

00:39:24.500 --> 00:39:28.920
is that once people
kinda buy into a show--

00:39:28.920 --> 00:39:30.300
A channel, really.

00:39:30.300 --> 00:39:34.370
A channel, because really,
on YouTube channels,

00:39:34.370 --> 00:39:37.810
are shows, like people try to
do multiple shows on channels

00:39:37.810 --> 00:39:42.810
and there are exceptions and
we've been able launch Josh's

00:39:42.830 --> 00:39:46.120
channel via shows on the weekends on GMM.

00:39:46.120 --> 00:39:46.953
In general, people--

00:39:46.953 --> 00:39:49.500
Subscribe to Mythical
Kitchen, click that bell.

00:39:49.500 --> 00:39:52.670
In general, people will kind
of interpret channels as,

00:39:52.670 --> 00:39:55.010
this is a show and it has
kind of a certain format

00:39:55.010 --> 00:39:56.840
that I can kind of expect.

00:39:56.840 --> 00:39:59.740
Anything different is
confusing and you also don't,

00:39:59.740 --> 00:40:03.160
if it under performs for
reasons like, who knows how the

00:40:03.160 --> 00:40:06.280
